## Key Data Exploration Findings

1. **Changes are rare:** Only 255 cell-month transitions involve a control change
   across the full 29-month dataset. Change rate: ~1% of all cell-months.

2. **Changes cluster in time:** Most changes happened in early-to-mid 2024
   (peak: August 2024 with 38 changes — likely Operation 1027 aftermath).
   Late 2025/early 2026 validation period is relatively quiet.

3. **Changes cluster in space:** Changes concentrate on specific frontlines.
   94 out of 185 cells change at least once. Some cells change up to 12 times.

4. **Class persistence varies:**
   - Government (gov): mean spell length 16.4 months — very sticky
   - Opposition (opo): mean spell length 8.4 months
   - Uncertain: mean spell length 7.9 months

5. **Spatial waves:** When a cell changes, on average 0.8 neighboring cells
   also changed in the same month. Changes propagate spatially.

6. **Most common transitions:**
   - gov → opo: 69 events (government losing ground)
   - opo → gov: 49 events (government recapturing)
   - uncertain → gov/opo: 87 events (contested zones resolving)

