## The U-Net Model (Tizian's work)

### Architecture
- Framework: `segmentation_models_pytorch`
- Encoder: ResNet-34 pretrained on ImageNet
- Input: 10 channels (UCDP features), raster size 40×16 (padded)
- Output: 3-class prediction map (gov/opo/uncertain) per cell
- Total parameters: 22M (encoder 21.3M, decoder+head 0.8M)

### Training Strategy
- Phase 1 (epochs 1-30): encoder frozen, only decoder trains
- Phase 2 (epochs 31-200): encoder unfrozen at lr=1e-5
- Loss: 0.5 × weighted CrossEntropy + 0.5 × Dice loss
- Optimizer: Adam, lr=1e-4, weight decay=1e-5
- Class weights: inverse frequency

### Single Split Results (train ≤ Sep 2025, val Oct 2025 - Mar 2026)
| Model | Accuracy | Macro F1 |
|-------|----------|---------|
| Majority class baseline | 0.608 | 0.257 |
| Random Forest (tabular) | 0.537 | 0.354 |
| No-change baseline | 0.972 | 0.967 |
| **U-Net (200 epochs)** | **0.918** | **0.899** |

### The Critical Problem
The no-change baseline (predict same label as last month) gets **macro F1 0.967**,
beating the U-Net's 0.899. This is because 97% of cell-months are stable —
the model is largely memorising geography rather than learning dynamics.

