The most meaningful evaluation: restrict to the 255 cell-months where control
actually changed. No-change scores 0% by definition on these rows.

| Fold | Cutoff | Change events | U-Net accuracy | Random (1/3 classes) |
|------|--------|--------------|---------------|---------------------|
| 1 | 2024-03 | 181 | 0.315 | 0.333 |
| 2 | 2024-07 | 122 | 0.328 | 0.333 |
| 3 | 2024-09 | 81 | 0.407 | 0.333 |
| 4 | 2025-03 | 59 | 0.390 | 0.333 |
| 5 | 2025-09 | 31 | 0.484 | 0.333 |

**Mean U-Net accuracy on change events: 0.385**
**No-change baseline: 0.000 by definition**

The U-Net beats random guessing on change events, and improves with more training
data. But performance is limited by the small number of change events available.

