## Pre-Coup Temporal Validation

**Test:** Feed the trained U-Net (fold 5) with UCDP features averaged over 2018-2020
(pre-coup baseline) and compare predictions against November 2023 ground truth.

**Motivation:** If the model learned a general conflict-to-control relationship,
pre-coup conflict patterns should still roughly predict post-coup control geography
(same actors, same geographic dynamics, just different intensity).

**Result:**
- Accuracy: 0.553 (majority class baseline: 0.561)
- Macro F1: 0.393
- The model essentially defaults to predicting government everywhere
- 41 pre-coup cells had any conflict activity vs 185 labeled cells
- `uncertain` recall collapses to 11% — model has no idea where contested zones will be

**Interpretation:** The model has not learned a generalizable conflict-to-control
relationship. It learned the specific post-coup geography. With pre-coup inputs
(lower intensity, different spatial distribution) it falls back to near-majority-class
prediction. This is an important limitation for generalization to new conflicts.

