## Known Limitations

1. **Temporal coverage:** Only 29 months of ground truth labels (Nov 2023 - Mar 2026).
   Pre-coup Wikipedia SVGs do not exist. Insufficient for robust change prediction.

2. **Label quality:** Wikipedia is crowd-sourced, may lag real events by ~5 weeks.
   Single editor's judgment. Some icon ambiguity (KIO/KIA, MNDAA, PSLF/TNLA share icons).

3. **No-change dominance:** 97% of cell-months are stable. Any model evaluated on
   aggregate metrics will be dominated by the no-change baseline.

4. **Small change events:** Only 255 change events across 29 months. Validation sets
   for change prediction are too small for statistically robust conclusions.

5. **Geographic memorisation:** U-Net appears to learn stable geographic patterns
   rather than dynamic conflict-to-control relationships (confirmed by pre-coup test).

6. **LOCF assumption:** Labels are forward-filled between Wikipedia snapshots.
   Actual changes between snapshots are invisible.

7. **No true test set:** 29-month constraint makes 3-way train/val/test split infeasible.

8. **SVG georeferencing:** ~4-6km error from pixel-to-coordinate interpolation.
   SVG approach not used as primary labels for this reason.

