## Supervisor Guidance (Mihai Croicu)

Key feedback received:

- **The no-change baseline must be beaten.** Any model that doesn't beat "predict
  same as last month" is not adding value. This is the hard benchmark.

- **Evaluate on changing cells specifically.** Overall accuracy is misleading.
  The interesting question is: when something changes, does the model know?

- **Spatial cross-validation is the right test.** Train on half the country,
  predict the other half. If it works, the model learned dynamics. If not,
  it memorised geography.

- **More training data is the bottleneck.** With only 29 months of labels,
  early folds have too little training data and later folds have too little
  validation data.

- **Don't go to Nigeria yet.** Nail Myanmar first. One naive application as
  a discussion plot is sufficient.

- **The U-Net image framing is theoretically right.** Territorial control is
  a spatial phenomenon. CNN kernels handle spatial lag automatically.
  But watch for overfitting given the small dataset (only 23-29 training rasters).

- **Descriptive statistics of cell changes first.** How many cells change,
  after how much time, with how many neighbors changing simultaneously —
  these geostatistics should precede any modelling.